#### Example:

```javascript
function greet(city) {
  console.log(this.name + " from " + city);
}

const user1 = { name: "Vasanth" };
const user2 = { name: "Rahul" };
```

1️⃣ bind creates a new function

```javascript
const boundGreet = greet.bind(user1);
console.log(boundGreet === greet); // false
```

2️⃣ this is permanently fixed

```javascript
boundGreet("Bengaluru");
output: "Vasanth from Bengaluru"
```

3️⃣ Cannot be overridden by call or apply

```javascript
boundGreet.call(user2, "Mumbai");
boundGreet.apply(user2, ["Delhi"]);
```

Output both times:

```javascript
Vasanth from Mumbai
Vasanth from Delhi
```

⚠️ Even though we passed user2, this did not change.

### Hook Composition (Very Important)

Custom hooks can use other custom hooks.

```javascript
function useUserProfile(userId) {
  const user = useFetchUser(userId);
  const isOnline = useOnlineStatus();

return { user, isOnline };
}
```

---

#### Root router composes them

```javascript
// app/router.tsx
<Routes>
  {authRoutes}
  {dashboardRoutes}
  {profileRoutes}
</Routes>
```

> Root router only composes — it does not define features.

